<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for your application to travel with your dog, [<strong>insert dog name</strong>] in the aircraft cabin with Qantas.<br />
<br />
Qantas must be satisfied that it is safe to carry your dog in the aircraft cabin.<br />
<br />
 We are unable to grant permission for your dog, [<strong>insert dog name</strong>] to travel in the aircraft cabin at this time because: [<strong>delete the items that are not applicable</strong>]
<ul>
	<li>Your dog is not neutered.</li>
	<li>Your dog weighs more than 45kg and does not meet the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs.html">Criteria for Carriage</a>&nbsp;of a Service Dog.</li>
	<li>Your dog exceeds the length limit for the aircraft operating and therefore does not meet the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs.html">Criteria for Carriage</a>&nbsp;of a Service Dog.</li>
	<li>You have not provided current/valid identification.</li>
	<li>Your dog has not been trained and/or certified or accredited by a training organisation or trainer that is a full member of <a href="https://assistancedogsinternational.org/resources/member-search/">Assistance Dogs International</a> (ADI) or is approved under the <a href="https://www.tatsipca.qld.gov.au/">Queensland Guide, Hearing and Assistance Dogs Act 2009</a> (Queensland Act).</li>
	<li>You have not provided suitable evidence or documentation to support your application.</li>
	<li>Your dog does not meet the <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/specific-needs/travelling-with-specific-needs/service-dogs.html">Criteria for Carriage</a> of a Service Dog under Training.</li>
</ul>
To consider your application further, please complete and attach the&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/content/dam/qantas/pdfs/fly/specific-needs/service-dogs/more-information-form.pdf">More Information</a>&nbsp;form and reply to this email along with supporting documentation. Please provide this information at least 14 days prior to travel to assist Qantas to determine if it is safe to carry the [<strong>Service Dog/Service Dog Under Training</strong>] in the aircraft cabin.<br />
<br />
 As you are currently unable to travel with your dog in the cabin, we can explore alternatives with you, including the offer of a full refund for any flights you have booked but not yet undertaken. If your dog is not approved to travel in the aircraft cabin it may still travel with Qantas, however carriage must be in the aircraft’s cargo hold in accordance with <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/travel-info/travelling-with-pets.html">Qantas Freight requirements</a>.</body>
</html>